# Layout versions

Raidwise uses **layout versions** (`vN` badges) separate from addon semver (`Addon.version`).

## When to bump

Bump the relevant `*_LAYOUT_VERSION` or page `LAYOUT_VERSION` when you change:

- Frame structure (new/removed panels, tabs, columns)
- Control layout or geometry (anchors, sizes, scroll areas)
- Named frames that must be recreated (`RaidwiseExportScroll`, profile tag scroll, etc.)
- Shared theme sizes in `Addon.UITheme` that affect an existing view

Do **not** bump for:

- Locale / string-only edits (`Locale.lua`, `RefreshLocalizedUI` text)
- Data-only logic (roster builders, export JSON, lockout math)
- Color tweaks that do not change layout geometry (prefer semver PATCH if user-visible)

## Where constants live

| View | Constant | Module |
|------|----------|--------|
| Main shell | `SHELL_LAYOUT_VERSION` | `ExporterWindow.lua` |
| Profile popup | `PROFILE_LAYOUT_VERSION` | `CharacterProfile.lua` |
| Content pages | `LAYOUT_VERSION` on `Addon.Pages.*` | `Page*.lua` |

## After bumping

1. Stamp `frame.layoutVersion` or `page.layoutVersion` in `Create`.
2. Show badge via `Addon.Widgets.AttachLayoutVersionLabel` (title bar) or `AttachPageLayoutBadge` (page toolbar).
3. Ensure rebuild logic compares stored version to registered constant (shell + profile already do).
4. Update the layout table in `docs/UI-Views.md`.
5. Update affected sizes in `docs/UI-Sizes.md` when pixels change.

## Versioning guidance

- Start new views at `LAYOUT_VERSION = 1`.
- Increment by 1 per structural change (no semver coupling).
- Profile layout can jump (currently `22`) when large profile refactors ship; keep one constant per profile window generation.
